Checklist item answers:
ItemTitle: Does the escapeStringValue implementation correctly prioritize backslash escaping before quotes to avoid double-escaping vulnerabilities?
Answer:
ChecklistItemAnswer[finalAnswer=Yes, the escapeStringValue implementation correctly prioritizes backslash escaping before quotes to avoid double-escaping vulnerabilities., analysis=The escapeStringValue method explicitly escapes backslashes first using replace("\\", "\\\\"), then escapes quotes using replace("\"", "\\\"). This ensures backslashes are escaped before quotes, preventing double-escaping. The implementation matches the checklist requirement of prioritizing backslash escaping before quotes., evidence=[EvidenceItem[file=spring-ai-vector-store/src/main/java/org/springframework/ai/vectorstore/filter/converter/AbstractFilterExpressionConverter.java, lines=210-213, reason=The escapeStringValue method replaces backslashes first, then quotes, ensuring backslashes are escaped before quotes to avoid double-escaping.], EvidenceItem[file=spring-ai-vector-store/src/main/java/org/springframework/ai/vectorstore/filter/converter/AbstractFilterExpressionConverter.java, lines=215-216, reason=The method uses replace("\\", "\\\\") to escape backslashes, which is required to avoid double-escaping when followed by quote escaping.], EvidenceItem[file=spring-ai-vector-store/src/main/java/org/springframework/ai/vectorstore/filter/converter/AbstractFilterExpressionConverter.java, lines=217-218, reason=The method uses replace("\"", "\\\") to escape quotes, which is applied after backslash escaping, maintaining correct priority.]]]
