ItemTitle: Are all string literals in filter expressions now wrapped in the appropriate escaping methods (e.g., escapeSqlStringValue, escapeODataStringValue, escapeSpELStringValue) to prevent syntax breakage?
Answer:
ChecklistItemAnswer[finalAnswer=Yes, all string literals in filter expressions are now wrapped in the appropriate escaping methods to prevent syntax breakage and injection attacks., analysis=All string literals in filter expressions are now wrapped in appropriate escaping methods (escapeStringValue, escapeODataStringValue, escapeSqlStringValue) as required. The code explicitly uses these methods to escape special characters and prevent syntax breakage or injection attacks. The methods are defined to handle specific escaping rules for each format (JSON/SpEL, SQL, OData, Weaviate)., evidence=[EvidenceItem[file=spring-ai-vector-store/src/main/java/org/springframework/ai/vectorstore/filter/converter/AbstractFilterExpressionConverter.java, lines=145-152, reason=The code now uses escapeStringValue(s) to wrap string values in double quotes, preventing syntax breakage by escaping quotes and backslashes.], EvidenceItem[file=spring-ai-vector-store/src/main/java/org/springframework/ai/vectorstore/filter/converter/AbstractFilterExpressionConverter.java, lines=210-218, reason=The escapeStringValue method is defined to replace backslashes and double quotes, ensuring safe string representation in filter expressions.], EvidenceItem[file=vector-stores/spring-ai-mariadb-store/src/main/java/org/springframework/ai/vectorstore/mariadb/MariaDBFilterExpressionConverter.java, lines=47-52, reason=The code now uses escapeSqlStringValue(s) to wrap string values in single quotes with escaped quotes and backslashes, preventing SQL injection.], EvidenceItem[file=vector-stores/spring-ai-mariadb-store/src/main/java/org/springframework/ai/vectorstore/mariadb/MariaDBFilterExpressionConverter.java, lines=53-60, reason=The escapeSqlStringValue method is defined to replace backslashes and single quotes, ensuring safe SQL string literals.], EvidenceItem[file=vector-stores/spring-ai-azure-store/src/main/java/org/springframework/ai/vectorstore/azure/AzureAiSearchFilterExpressionConverter.java, lines=151-158, reason=The code now uses escapeODataStringValue(text) to wrap string values in single quotes with escaped quotes, preventing OData injection.], EvidenceItem[file=vector-stores/spring-ai-azure-store/src/main/java/org/springframework/ai/vectorstore/azure/AzureAiSearchFilterExpressionConverter.java, lines=160-167, reason=The escapeODataStringValue method is defined to replace single quotes with doubled quotes, ensuring safe OData string literals.], EvidenceItem[file=vector-stores/spring-ai-weaviate-store/src/main/java/org/springframework/ai/vectorstore/weaviate/WeaviateFilterExpressionConverter.java, lines=182-188, reason=The code now uses escapeStringValue(s) to wrap string values in double quotes with escaped quotes and backslashes, preventing syntax breakage.], EvidenceItem[file=vector-stores/spring-ai-weaviate-store/src/main/java/org/springframework/ai/vectorstore/weaviate/WeaviateFilterExpressionConverter.java, lines=190-197, reason=The escapeStringValue method is defined to replace backslashes and double quotes, ensuring safe valueText format.]]]
